terms (raw show / prettyShow)
==========
x0:  show=x0  pretty=X
x1:  show=x1  pretty=Y
Int:  show=TyCon Int  pretty=Int
Int->Bool:  show=Arrow(TyCon Int,TyCon Bool)  pretty=Int -> Bool
A->B:  show=Arrow(x0,x1)  pretty=X -> Y
A->A:  show=Arrow(x0,x0)  pretty=X -> X

match pat term  (one-sided: vars in pat bind to subterms of term)
==========
match A     Int          = {X -> Int}
match A->B  Int->Bool    = {X -> Int, Y -> Bool}
match A->A  Int->Bool    = Nothing
match Int   A            = Nothing

unify  (two-sided: vars on either side can bind)
==========
unify A     Int          = {X -> Int}
unify A->B  Int->Bool    = {X -> Int, Y -> Bool}
unify A->A  Int->Bool    = Nothing
unify A->B  Int->A       = {X -> Int, Y -> Int}

applying a substitution
==========
sub = unify (A->B) (Int->Bool) = {X -> Int, Y -> Bool}
apply sub to (A->B):  Int -> Bool
apply sub to (A->A):  Int -> Int
apply sub to Char:    Char
